  "summary": "A distinctive body painting tradition of the Turkana people using natural pigments to create symbolic patterns on skin and objects.",
  "description": "The aesthetic features white, red, and ochre geometric patterns applied to faces, bodies, and personal items using natural pigments from ochre, charcoal, and clay. These designs communicate identity, age-set affiliation, and social status within Turkana society.",
